{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-glossary-s3-group","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:glossary-s3-group","kind":"remark","title":"Symmetric group $S_3$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-braid-group"],"tags":["glossary","symmetric-group","group-theory"],"defines":["s3-group"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.S3Group","text":"glossary-s3-group.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/glossary/glossary-s3-group.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:glossary-s3-group\"></a><p>Imposing the involution relations <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_i^2=\\mathrm{id}</code> on the braid group <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B_3</code> yields the <strong><dfn class=\"defterm\" id=\"term-s3-group\">symmetric group <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S_3</code></dfn></strong>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">S_3\n  =\\bigl\\langle s_1,s_2\n     \\big| s_1^2=s_2^2=(s_1 s_2)^3=\\mathrm{id}\\bigr\\rangle.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/glossary/glossary-s3-group.md","heading":"Remark","number":"24.6.1"}
